{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The C API exposes only `read_side_info`; `get_bits` is internal. Its meaningful valid-path axes are MPEG-1 versus MPEG-2/2.5 parsing, mono versus non-mono granule count, sample-rate table selection, switched versus normal windows, switched block types, mixed versus pure short blocks, starting bit alignment, and the non-MPEG-1 `scalefac_compress >= 500` preflag threshold. The explicit rejection surface has three branches: `big_values > 288`, switched-window `block_type == 0`, and the final bit-budget check."}}
